renovate: a branch with nothing to commit isn't pending on the dashboard

processBranch returns `no-work` with no branch when an update turns out to
change nothing (a lock file refresh whose lock is already current). The
dashboard didn't know the branch was absent and listed it under Other
Branches, "pending", every run of its schedule, though there's nothing a
PR could bring. A run now keeps whether each branch exists, and the
dashboard leaves out a no-work branch that doesn't.

--- a/lib/workers/repository/dependency-dashboard.ts
+++ b/lib/workers/repository/dependency-dashboard.ts
@@ -362,6 +362,9 @@
   const branches = allBranches.filter(
     (branch) =>
       branch.result !== 'automerged' &&
+      // Nothing to commit and no branch: the update is already in (a lock
+      // file refresh that changes nothing), so it isn't pending.
+      !(branch.result === 'no-work' && branch.branchExists === false) &&
       !branch.upgrades?.every((upgrade) => upgrade.remediationNotPossible),
   );
   if (!(
